<title>GERMANY: Toepfer maintains higher German grain forecast.</title>
<headline>Toepfer maintains higher German grain forecast.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's 1997 grain harvest will exceed the 1996 result of 42.1 million tonnes if the weather remains stable and if enough rain is received, grain trader Toepfer said in a monthly newsletter.</p>
<p>It said the area had been raised by five percent and crop conditions in western and northern Germany were good although some regional dry spells had left their mark.</p>
<p>Precipitation in the first half of May had filled upper soil layers with enough moisture but lower layers up to a depth of 60 centimetres could still do with more rain, Toepfer added.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
